+## Render helper selection
+
+Always use the **lightest** helper that satisfies the component's dependencies. Never reach for a heavier utility when a simpler one works.
+
+| Component needs                                      | Helper to use                | Import                                                 |
+| ---------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |
+| Nothing (pure/presentational)                        | `render`                     | `vitest-browser-react`                                 |
+| Router only (`useNavigate`, `useParams`, links…)     | `renderWithRouter`           | `@/test/browser-test-utils/renderWithRouter`           |
+| TanStack Query only (`useQuery`, `useMutation`…)     | `renderWithQuery`            | `@/test/browser-test-utils/renderWithQuery`            |
+| React Hook Form context only                         | `renderWithForm`             | `@/test/browser-test-utils/renderWithForm`             |
+| React Hook Form + Redux (or Router)                  | `renderWithFormAndProviders` | `@/test/browser-test-utils/renderWithFormAndProviders` |
+| Redux state/selectors (with or without Router/Query) | `renderWithProviders`        | `@/test/browser-test-utils/renderWithProviders`        |
+
+`renderWithProviders` is the **last resort** — only when the component reads from or dispatches to the Redux store. Passing `withQueryClient: true` or `withRouter: false` is fine when Redux is already required.
+
+```ts
+// Pure component — no providers needed
+function renderComponent(props = defaultProps) {
+  return render(<MyComponent {...props} />);
+}
+
+// Needs routing only
+function renderComponent(props = defaultProps) {
+  return renderWithRouter(<MyComponent {...props} />, { pathname: '/some/path' });
+}
+
+// Needs TanStack Query only
+function renderComponent(props = defaultProps) {
+  return renderWithQuery(<MyComponent {...props} />);
+}
+
+// Needs React Hook Form context only
